        "text": "break statement",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "When Java sees the break statement it will ignore everything else after and it will terminate the loop.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "continue statement",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "When Java sees the continue statement it moves control to the beginning of the loop, causing the remaining statements in the current iteration to be ignored.",
        "refs": ["Q0003"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "The break statement terminates a loop.",
        "refs": ["Q0004"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "The continue statement moves control to the beginning of a loop.",
        "refs": ["Q0004"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Using `true` as the loop condition creates an infinite loop that runs until a break statement terminates it.",
        "refs": ["Q0004", "Q0005"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
  ],
